icitly cleaning.  \n→ **Conclusion:** She performs at least one clear housework activity: watering plants.\n\n---\n\n### 4) Does she go to the gym?\n\n❌ **No.**  \nThere is no visual evidence of her going to the gym, exercising, or engaging in any physical workout activity in these frames.\n\n---\n\n### 5) Does she go back to sleep?\n\n❌ **No.**  \nShe remains active throughout all 30 frames, performing various tasks. There is no indication she returns to bed or sleeps again.\n\n---\n\n### Temporal Sequence of Activities:\n\n1. **Frames 1–7:** She interacts with a humidifier and a glowing lamp — likely part of a morning self-care or relaxation ritual.\n2. **Frames 8–17:** She waters plants — housework/garden maintenance.\n3. **Frames 18–29:** She moves to the kitchen, opens the fridge, and retrieves items — likely preparing for a meal or drink.\n4. **Frame 30:** She prepares a hot beverage on a cooktop — part of breakfast preparation.\n\n---\n\n### Final Evaluation of Answer “3”:\n\n> “She gets up, cooks her breakfast and does some housework”\n\n- ✅ Gets up — Confirmed.\n- ⚠️ Cooks her breakfast — Partially confirmed (prepares a hot drink, but no solid food cooking shown).\n- ✅ Does some housework — Confirmed (watering plants).\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Verdict: **Answer ‘3’ is mostly correct.**\n\nIt accurately describes the woman’s activities as being awake, doing housework (watering plants), and preparing part of breakfast (a hot drink). While “cooks her breakfast” is slightly overstated (since no actual cooking of food is shown), it is reasonable to interpret beverage preparation as part of a breakfast routine in this context. The answer aligns well with the visual evidence provided.'}, {'batch_start': 180, 'batch_end': 210, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/jp2M1hIEtsk/frames/frame_0436.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/jp2M1hIEtsk/frames/frame_0437.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/jp2M1hIEtsk/frames/frame_0438.jpg', '/mnt/s