rocessed/jp2M1hIEtsk/frames/frame_0623.jpg'], 'response': 'Based on the provided frames (00:00–14:00), let’s analyze the answer “3: She gets up, cooks her breakfast and does some housework” by checking each criterion:\n\n---\n\n**1) Is the woman awake and out of bed?**  \n✅ **Yes.**  \nWhile there is no explicit shot of her getting out of bed, all frames from 00:00–14:00 show her fully dressed (in a sweater and pants), actively moving around the kitchen and bathroom, preparing food, and cleaning. This strongly implies she is awake and has started her day. The context of the full video summary (morning routine, tea/coffee, etc.) further supports this.\n\n---\n\n**2) Does she cook/prepare breakfast?**  \n✅ **Yes.**  \nFrames 0436–0445 show her preparing a blended drink:  \n- She stirs a liquid in a mug (0436).  \n- She pours a creamy liquid (likely milk or yogurt) into a blender (0437–0441).  \n- She adds sliced kiwi (0443–0445).  \nThis is consistent with preparing a smoothie or blended breakfast beverage — a common breakfast activity. Though not “cooking” in the traditional sense (e.g., frying eggs), food preparation for breakfast is clearly occurring.\n\n---\n\n**3) Does she do housework (cleaning, organizing, etc.)?**  \n✅ **Yes.**  \nMultiple frames show housework:  \n- **Dishwashing:** Frames 0476–0485 show her wearing yellow gloves, scrubbing dishes in the sink with soap and water.  \n- **Mopping:** Frames 0615–0621 show a mop cleaning the floor, and the woman is visible holding the mop handle, actively mopping.  \n- **Bathroom cleaning:** Frames 0622–0623 show her wiping down a bathroom sink with a cloth.  \nThese are all clear examples of housework.\n\n---\n\n**4) Does she go to the gym?**  \n❌ **No.**  \nThere is no visual evidence in any of the 30 frames of her going to or being at a gym. No workout equipment, gym setting, or exercise activity is shown.\n\n---\n\n**5) Does she go back to sleep?**  \n❌ **No.**  \nAll activities shown are active and daytime-o