g ritual rather than cooking or preparing a meal. There is no visible kitchen activity, stove, pan, or food preparation tools. The global summary mentions cooking later (e.g., sandwiches, fries), but **within these 30 frames, no breakfast preparation occurs.**\n\n---\n\n**3) Does she do housework (cleaning, organizing, etc.)?**\n\n✅ **Partially — organizing clothes.**  \nIn Frames 24–30, the woman opens a closet and browses through hanging clothes, touching and shifting garments. This can be interpreted as organizing or selecting an outfit — a form of light housework or personal organization. However, there is no evidence of cleaning (e.g., sweeping, wiping surfaces, laundry) in these frames.\n\n---\n\n**4) Does she go to the gym?**\n\n❌ **No.**  \nThere is no gym equipment, workout attire, or physical exercise shown in any of the frames. Her activities are entirely domestic and sedentary.\n\n---\n\n**5) Does she go back to sleep?**\n\n❌ **No.**  \nShe remains active throughout all 30 frames — drinking water, lighting a candle, using her phone, and organizing clothes. No return to bed or signs of sleeping are visible.\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Sequence of Activities in These Frames:**\n\n- **Frames 1–2:** Close-up of lemon water, then woman at counter pouring water.\n- **Frames 3–8:** Woman lighting a candle with a match, placing it on the counter.\n- **Frames 9–12:** Candle burning next to digital clock showing 5:16.\n- **Frames 13–19:** Woman drinking lemon water.\n- **Frames 20–22:** Woman using her smartphone.\n- **Frames 23:** Empty desk and chair — transition shot.\n- **Frames 24–30:** Woman walks to closet, opens it, and browses clothes.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe answer “She gets up, cooks her breakfast and does some housework” is **partially correct but misleading** for this segment.\n\n- ✅ She is awake and out of bed — **Correct.**\n- ❌ She does **not** cook or prepare breakfast in these frames — **Incorrect.**\n- ✅ She does **some** housework (organizing