, gym equipment, workout attire, or any activity related to fitness in these frames.\n\n---\n\n**5) Does she go back to sleep?**\n\n❌ **No.** The woman is continuously active throughout the frames. The bed is shown unmade in frame 27, but she is not seen returning to it or lying down. All her actions suggest she is engaged in chores, not resting.\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Sequence of Activities (within these frames):**\n\n- **Frames 1-5:** Close-up of ironing setup — adjusting cord, placing iron on board. (Preparation)\n- **Frames 6-10:** Ironing a white shirt, then holding it up.\n- **Frames 11-16:** Hanging the freshly ironed shirt on a rack near a window.\n- **Frames 17-21:** Ironing a black skirt, then a patterned scarf or fabric.\n- **Frames 22-26:** Standing near the ironing area, possibly preparing next item or moving around.\n- **Frames 27-30:** Static shot of the bedroom — unmade bed, clothes hanging — suggesting the chores are ongoing or recently completed.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe answer “She gets up, cooks her breakfast and does some housework” is **partially correct but misleading**.\n\n- ✅ She **gets up** — Confirmed.\n- ✅ She **does some housework** — Confirmed (ironing and hanging clothes).\n- ❌ She **cooks her breakfast** — **Not shown or supported** by any frame in this segment.\n\nTherefore, **answer \'3\' is not fully correct** for this segment. It incorrectly includes “cooks her breakfast,” which is not depicted in these frames. A more accurate description would be: “She gets up and does laundry-related housework (ironing and hanging clothes).”\n\nIf this 30-frame segment is representative of the broader 00:00-14:00 period, then the answer is still inaccurate unless cooking occurs outside this segment — but based solely on the provided frames, we must conclude the cooking part is unsupported.\n\n---\n\n**Final Verdict: Answer \'3\' is INCORRECT for the provided frames.**'}, {'batch_start': 150, 'batch_end': 180, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data